= Web browser =

== Overview ==
A '''web browser''' is a user-agent application that retrieves, interprets, presents, and interacts with Web resources.

Browsers resolve resource identifiers, issue Web requests, process representations such as HTML, execute supported scripts, enforce security policies, and provide user interfaces for navigation and interaction.

A browser is not a search engine. Search engines index and retrieve information; browsers are general clients used to access Web resources, including search engines.

== Boundaries ==
* web browser ≠ search engine
* browser ≠ Web itself
* rendered page ≠ source representation alone

